    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a2">

                <pb facs="0260" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg254"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seat to Mr. Braida.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consular Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bluefields, Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: Since closing a dispatch forwarded
                    to you this morning by the hands of Mr. William English, I have been called into
                    a meeting of the American residents at the clubroom. The local complications are
                    such that your presence is considered indispensable. They send a delegation on
                    board the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Yulu</hi> to bring you to
                    Bluefields. Permit me, in their behalf and on my own account, to respectfully
                    urge you to comply with their wishes and return with them.</p>
                <p>Hoping to see you on the return of the <hi rendition="#italic">Yulu.</hi></p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. B. Seat</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consular Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
